# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Affordable Remodeling — environment variables
#
# The site currently requires NO environment variables to build or run:
# it is a fully static build (npm run build -> dist/).
#
# The variables below are RESERVED for when the contact form is wired to
# a real inbox (see README "Wire the contact form"). Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Formspree form ID for the contact/estimate form (e.g. "abcdwxyz").
# Create one at https://formspree.io, then set this in Vercel:
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
# VITE_FORMSPREE_ID=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI website assistant (the "Ask us" chat bubble)
#
# Set this in Vercel -> Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
# NOT prefixed with VITE_ on purpose: VITE_ variables are inlined into the
# browser bundle, which would publish the key to every visitor. This one is
# read only inside api/chat.js, server-side.
#
# Without it, /api/chat answers 501 and the chat widget tells visitors to
# call instead of pretending to be online.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Optional model override (defaults to claude-haiku-4-5-20251001):
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owner console (/owner) — connect the site's forms to a CRM
#
# OWNER_PASSWORD is the only credential guarding /owner. Until it is set,
# the page renders but nobody can sign in, which is the safe default.
# Make it long; it is the whole lock.
# OWNER_PASSWORD=
#
# Optional. If unset, the session cookie is signed with a key derived from
# OWNER_PASSWORD, which means changing the password signs everyone out.
# Set this only if you want to rotate sessions without changing the password.
# OWNER_SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Storage for the CRM settings the owner saves. Create an Upstash for Redis
# database from the project's Storage tab and connect it — Vercel injects
# KV_REST_API_URL and KV_REST_API_TOKEN for you. Without them the console
# loads but says, honestly, that nothing can be saved yet.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
